Chapter: CellEval
  cites Sheets chapter CellGraph
  cites Sheets chapter CellFormula
  cites Sheets chapter CellStore
  cites Foreword chapter CCE

 Evaluation in the order CellGraph derived, and the function set in the
 order the register stages it: arithmetic and comparison, aggregates over
 ranges, conditionals, text.

 A FORMULA IS TYPED. `=A1+B1` where B1 holds text is a refusal naming B1,
 never a silent zero and never a sigil inherited from 1985. A text value
 therefore carries WHERE IT CAME FROM: an operator sees values rather
 than expressions, so without the origin the refusal could only say that
 some operand was text, and a person reading a wrong total needs the
 cell.

 An error PROPAGATES unchanged rather than being reworded at each level,
 so the message that reaches the top names the cell that caused it and
 not the outermost operator.

 The choices a spreadsheet has to make, made:

 - An EMPTY cell is zero in arithmetic and is not counted by COUNT. A
   cell nobody filled is an absence, and absence in a sum is zero; a
   count of quantities that counted absences would answer the size of
   the range.
 - A RANGE SKIPS text and empty cells rather than refusing. A label
   sitting above a column of quantities is the normal shape of a sheet,
   and the refusal exists for `+`, where the operand was named
   deliberately.
 - MIN, MAX and AVERAGE over a range holding NO numbers refuse. An empty
   maximum has no honest value, and zero is the answer that looks right.
 - AVERAGE truncates, because a cell holds a 32-bit integer. The
   truncation is stated here rather than discovered.
 - SUMIF and COUNTIF take a VALUE to match, exactly, rather than a text
   criterion like ">5". A criterion parsed out of a string is a second
   expression language reachable only at runtime.

 LEN counts CODE POINTS, by skipping UTF-8 continuation bytes, because a
 person counting characters does not mean bytes. UPPER and LOWER fold
 ASCII only: every byte of a multi-byte sequence has its high bit set and
 is passed through untouched, so a non-ASCII character survives rather
 than being corrupted by a byte-wise fold. TRIM removes leading and
 trailing spaces and does not collapse runs inside.

 We say:

Section: Values

  TextVal = record {
    tv-text : Text,
    tv-from : Text
  }

  Value =
   | VNum (Integer)
   | VText (TextVal)
   | VErr (Text)
   | VEmpty

  Results = record {
    rs-ok : Boolean,
    rs-vals : List Value,
    rs-msg : Text
  }

  ev-lit : Text -> Value
  ev-lit (t) = VText (TextVal { tv-text = t, tv-from = "" })

  ev-from : Text, Text -> Value
  ev-from (t) (name) = VText (TextVal { tv-text = t, tv-from = name })

  ev-where : TextVal -> Text
  ev-where (v) = if (v.tv-from) == "" then "a text literal" else v.tv-from

  ev-is-err : Value -> Boolean
  ev-is-err (v) = when v
   is VErr (m) -> True
   is otherwise -> False

  ev-err-text : Value -> Text
  ev-err-text (v) = when v
   is VErr (m) -> m
   is otherwise -> ""

  ev-show : Value -> Text
  ev-show (v) = when v
   is VNum (n) -> show n
   is VText (t) -> t.tv-text
   is VErr (m) -> "REFUSED: " & m
   is VEmpty -> ""

  ev-is-empty : Value -> Boolean
  ev-is-empty (v) = when v
   is VEmpty -> True
   is otherwise -> False

  ev-cell-name : Integer, Integer -> Text
  ev-cell-name (r) (c) = gr-col-name c & show (r + 1)

Section: Reading A Cell

 A cell holding a formula answers the value already computed for it,
 which the derived order guarantees exists. Any other cell answers the
 store.

  ev-store : Program, Integer, Integer -> Value
  ev-store (pg) (r) (c) =
    let k = sheet-kind (pg.pg-blk) r c
    in if k == cs-number then VNum (sheet-get (pg.pg-blk) r c)
    else if k == cs-text then ev-from (sheet-text (pg.pg-blk) r c) (ev-cell-name r c)
    else VEmpty

  ev-cell : Program, List Value, Integer, Integer -> Value
  ev-cell (pg) (vals) (r) (c) =
    if sheet-in (pg.pg-blk) r c == False then VErr (ev-cell-name r c & " is outside the sheet")
    else let s = gr-slot-at pg r c
    in if s == 0 then ev-store pg r c
    else ev-named (list-at vals (s - 1)) (ev-cell-name r c)

 A text arriving from a formula cell is relabelled with the cell the
 reader named, because the origin a refusal should print is the cell in
 the formula and not whatever cell that formula copied its text from.

  ev-named : Value, Text -> Value
  ev-named (v) (name) = when v
   is VText (t) -> ev-from (t.tv-text) name
   is otherwise -> v

Section: Arithmetic And Comparison

  ev-need-num : Value, Text -> Text
  ev-need-num (v) (op) = when v
   is VText (t) -> ev-where t & " holds text, and " & op & " wants a number"
   is otherwise -> ""

  ev-num-of : Value -> Integer
  ev-num-of (v) = when v
   is VNum (n) -> n
   is otherwise -> 0

  ev-arith : Integer, Value, Value -> Value
  ev-arith (op) (a) (b) =
    let ta = ev-need-num a (fx-op-name op)
    in if ta /= "" then VErr ta
    else let tb = ev-need-num b (fx-op-name op)
    in if tb /= "" then VErr tb
    else ev-arith-do op (ev-num-of a) (ev-num-of b)

  ev-arith-do : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Value
  ev-arith-do (op) (a) (b) =
    if op == fx-op-add then VNum (a + b)
    else if op == fx-op-sub then VNum (a - b)
    else if op == fx-op-mul then VNum (a * b)
    else if b == 0 then VErr "division by zero"
    else VNum (a / b)

  ev-bool : Boolean -> Value
  ev-bool (b) = if b then VNum 1 else VNum 0

 Two texts compare for equality and inequality only. An ORDERING on text
 is a collation decision, and a byte order pretending to be one is the
 answer that looks right until a reader meets a language.

  ev-text-of : Value -> Text
  ev-text-of (v) = when v
   is VText (t) -> t.tv-text
   is otherwise -> ""

  ev-is-text : Value -> Boolean
  ev-is-text (v) = when v
   is VText (t) -> True
   is otherwise -> False

  ev-cmp : Integer, Value, Value -> Value
  ev-cmp (op) (a) (b) =
    if ev-is-text a & ev-is-text b then ev-cmp-text op a b
    else ev-cmp-num op a b

  ev-cmp-text : Integer, Value, Value -> Value
  ev-cmp-text (op) (a) (b) =
    if op == fx-op-eq then ev-bool (ev-text-of a == ev-text-of b)
    else if op == fx-op-ne then ev-bool (ev-text-of a /= ev-text-of b)
    else VErr ("text has no ordering, and " & fx-op-name op & " asked for one")

  ev-cmp-num : Integer, Value, Value -> Value
  ev-cmp-num (op) (a) (b) =
    let ta = ev-need-num a (fx-op-name op)
    in if ta /= "" then VErr ta
    else let tb = ev-need-num b (fx-op-name op)
    in if tb /= "" then VErr tb
    else ev-cmp-do op (ev-num-of a) (ev-num-of b)

  ev-cmp-do : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Value
  ev-cmp-do (op) (a) (b) =
    if op == fx-op-eq then ev-bool (a == b)
    else if op == fx-op-ne then ev-bool (a /= b)
    else if op == fx-op-lt then ev-bool (a < b)
    else if op == fx-op-gt then ev-bool (a > b)
    else if op == fx-op-le then ev-bool (a <= b)
    else ev-bool (a >= b)

  ev-is-cmp : Integer -> Boolean
  ev-is-cmp (op) = op >= fx-op-eq

  ev-binary : Integer, Value, Value -> Value
  ev-binary (op) (a) (b) =
    if ev-is-err a then a
    else if ev-is-err b then b
    else if ev-is-cmp op then ev-cmp op a b
    else ev-arith op a b

Section: Ranges

 A range is collected into a list of the NUMBERS it holds, so every
 aggregate is written over one traversal that has already made the
 skipping decision.

  ev-row-nums : Program, List Value, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  ev-row-nums (pg) (vals) (r) (c) (c2) (acc) =
    if c > c2 then acc
    else ev-row-nums pg vals r (c + 1) c2 (ev-take (ev-cell pg vals r c) acc)

  ev-take : Value, List Integer -> List Integer
  ev-take (v) (acc) = when v
   is VNum (n) -> list-push acc n
   is otherwise -> acc

  ev-rect-nums : Program, List Value, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  ev-rect-nums (pg) (vals) (r) (r2) (c) (c2) (acc) =
    if r > r2 then acc
    else ev-rect-nums pg vals (r + 1) r2 c c2 (ev-row-nums pg vals r c c2 acc)

  ev-range-nums : Program, List Value, RangeRef -> List Integer
  ev-range-nums (pg) (vals) (g) =
    let a = g.rr-from
    in let b = g.rr-to
    in ev-rect-nums pg vals (gr-lo (a.cr-row) (b.cr-row)) (gr-hi (a.cr-row) (b.cr-row)) (gr-lo (a.cr-col) (b.cr-col)) (gr-hi (a.cr-col) (b.cr-col)) []

 An empty cell is skipped by COUNT and is zero in a SUM, so a range's
 numbers are exactly what an aggregate reads. A cell holding an ERROR
 inside a range is not skipped: the error is the answer, because a total
 computed over a refusal is a wrong number wearing a right shape.

  ev-row-err : Program, List Value, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Value
  ev-row-err (pg) (vals) (r) (c) (c2) =
    if c > c2 then VNum 0
    else if ev-is-err (ev-cell pg vals r c) then ev-cell pg vals r c
    else ev-row-err pg vals r (c + 1) c2

  ev-rect-err : Program, List Value, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Value
  ev-rect-err (pg) (vals) (r) (r2) (c) (c2) =
    if r > r2 then VNum 0
    else if ev-is-err (ev-row-err pg vals r c c2) then ev-row-err pg vals r c c2
    else ev-rect-err pg vals (r + 1) r2 c c2

  ev-range-err : Program, List Value, RangeRef -> Value
  ev-range-err (pg) (vals) (g) =
    let a = g.rr-from
    in let b = g.rr-to
    in ev-rect-err pg vals (gr-lo (a.cr-row) (b.cr-row)) (gr-hi (a.cr-row) (b.cr-row)) (gr-lo (a.cr-col) (b.cr-col)) (gr-hi (a.cr-col) (b.cr-col))

  ev-sum-of : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ev-sum-of (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else ev-sum-of xs (i + 1) n (acc + list-at xs i)

  ev-min-of : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ev-min-of (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else if list-at xs i < acc then ev-min-of xs (i + 1) n (list-at xs i)
    else ev-min-of xs (i + 1) n acc

  ev-max-of : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ev-max-of (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else if list-at xs i > acc then ev-max-of xs (i + 1) n (list-at xs i)
    else ev-max-of xs (i + 1) n acc

Section: Text Functions

  ev-cont-byte : Integer -> Boolean
  ev-cont-byte (b) = b >= 128 & b < 192

  ev-len-of : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ev-len-of (bs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else if ev-cont-byte (list-at bs i) then ev-len-of bs (i + 1) n acc
    else ev-len-of bs (i + 1) n (acc + 1)

  ev-fold : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Boolean, List Integer -> List Integer
  ev-fold (bs) (i) (n) (up) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else ev-fold bs (i + 1) n up (list-push acc (ev-fold-byte (list-at bs i) up))

  ev-fold-byte : Integer, Boolean -> Integer
  ev-fold-byte (b) (up) =
    if up then (if b >= 97 & b <= 122 then b - 32 else b)
    else if b >= 65 & b <= 90 then b + 32
    else b

  ev-trim-start : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ev-trim-start (bs) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then i
    else if list-at bs i == 32 then ev-trim-start bs (i + 1) n
    else i

  ev-trim-end : List Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ev-trim-end (bs) (e) =
    if e <= 0 then e
    else if list-at bs (e - 1) == 32 then ev-trim-end bs (e - 1)
    else e

  ev-slice : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  ev-slice (bs) (i) (e) (acc) =
    if i >= e then acc
    else ev-slice bs (i + 1) e (list-push acc (list-at bs i))

Section: Calls

  ev-args : Program, List Value, List Expr, Integer, Integer, List Value -> List Value
  ev-args (pg) (vals) (args) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else ev-args pg vals args (i + 1) n (list-push acc (ev-expr pg vals (list-at args i)))

  ev-first-err : List Value, Integer, Integer -> Value
  ev-first-err (vs) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then VNum 0
    else if ev-is-err (list-at vs i) then list-at vs i
    else ev-first-err vs (i + 1) n

  ev-arity : Text, Integer, Integer -> Text
  ev-arity (nm) (want) (got) =
    nm & " wants " & show want & " arguments and was given " & show got

 A range argument is passed as an EXPRESSION rather than a value,
 because a range has no value of its own: only the aggregate reading it
 knows whether to sum the cells or count them.

  ev-range-arg : Expr -> Boolean
  ev-range-arg (e) = when e
   is ExRange (g) -> True
   is otherwise -> False

  ev-range-of : Expr -> RangeRef
  ev-range-of (e) = when e
   is ExRange (g) -> g
   is otherwise -> RangeRef { rr-from = CellRef { cr-row = 0, cr-col = 0, cr-name = "" }, rr-to = CellRef { cr-row = 0, cr-col = 0, cr-name = "" } }

  ev-agg : Program, List Value, Text, List Expr -> Value
  ev-agg (pg) (vals) (nm) (args) =
    if list-length args /= 1 then VErr (ev-arity nm 1 (list-length args))
    else if ev-range-arg (list-at args 0) == False then VErr (nm & " wants a range like A1:B9")
    else ev-agg-on pg vals nm (ev-range-of (list-at args 0))

  ev-agg-on : Program, List Value, Text, RangeRef -> Value
  ev-agg-on (pg) (vals) (nm) (g) =
    let bad = ev-range-err pg vals g
    in if ev-is-err bad then bad
    else ev-agg-nums nm (ev-range-nums pg vals g)

  ev-agg-nums : Text, List Integer -> Value
  ev-agg-nums (nm) (xs) =
    let n = list-length xs
    in if nm == "SUM" then VNum (ev-sum-of xs 0 n 0)
    else if nm == "COUNT" then VNum n
    else if n == 0 then VErr (nm & " has no numbers to work on")
    else if nm == "MIN" then VNum (ev-min-of xs 1 n (list-at xs 0))
    else if nm == "MAX" then VNum (ev-max-of xs 1 n (list-at xs 0))
    else VNum (ev-sum-of xs 0 n 0 / n)

  ev-match : Program, List Value, RangeRef, Value, Boolean -> Value
  ev-match (pg) (vals) (g) (want) (summing) =
    let bad = ev-range-err pg vals g
    in if ev-is-err bad then bad
    else ev-match-scan pg vals (ev-range-cells pg vals g) want summing

  ev-row-cells : Program, List Value, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Value -> List Value
  ev-row-cells (pg) (vals) (r) (c) (c2) (acc) =
    if c > c2 then acc
    else ev-row-cells pg vals r (c + 1) c2 (list-push acc (ev-cell pg vals r c))

  ev-rect-cells : Program, List Value, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Value -> List Value
  ev-rect-cells (pg) (vals) (r) (r2) (c) (c2) (acc) =
    if r > r2 then acc
    else ev-rect-cells pg vals (r + 1) r2 c c2 (ev-row-cells pg vals r c c2 acc)

  ev-range-cells : Program, List Value, RangeRef -> List Value
  ev-range-cells (pg) (vals) (g) =
    let a = g.rr-from
    in let b = g.rr-to
    in ev-rect-cells pg vals (gr-lo (a.cr-row) (b.cr-row)) (gr-hi (a.cr-row) (b.cr-row)) (gr-lo (a.cr-col) (b.cr-col)) (gr-hi (a.cr-col) (b.cr-col)) []

 An EMPTY cell matches only another empty, never the number zero: a
 COUNTIF for 0 that counted every unfilled cell in the range would
 answer the size of the range.

  ev-same : Value, Value -> Boolean
  ev-same (a) (b) =
    if ev-is-empty a | ev-is-empty b then ev-is-empty a & ev-is-empty b
    else if ev-is-text a & ev-is-text b then ev-text-of a == ev-text-of b
    else if ev-is-text a then False
    else if ev-is-text b then False
    else ev-num-of a == ev-num-of b

  ev-match-scan : Program, List Value, List Value, Value, Boolean -> Value
  ev-match-scan (pg) (vals) (cs) (want) (summing) =
    ev-match-loop cs 0 (list-length cs) want summing 0

  ev-match-loop : List Value, Integer, Integer, Value, Boolean, Integer -> Value
  ev-match-loop (cs) (i) (n) (want) (summing) (acc) =
    if i >= n then VNum acc
    else if ev-same (list-at cs i) want == False then ev-match-loop cs (i + 1) n want summing acc
    else if summing then ev-match-loop cs (i + 1) n want summing (acc + ev-num-of (list-at cs i))
    else ev-match-loop cs (i + 1) n want summing (acc + 1)

Section: Lookup

 `LOOKUP(range, key, header)`. The range's FIRST ROW is the header row
 and its FIRST COLUMN is the key column. The key is matched EXACTLY in
 the key column, and the answer is taken from the column whose header
 equals `header`.

 Named rather than positional, ruled 2026-09-08: a lookup keyed on
 column POSITION is wrong the first time somebody inserts a column, and
 nothing in the sheet says so.

 Three refusals, and each names what a person can act on: no column
 carries that header, no row carries that key, or MORE THAN ONE row
 carries that key. The last is the one other spreadsheets answer instead
 of refusing, and a duplicate key has no single right answer: taking the
 first is a near match wearing an exact match's clothes.

  ev-r1 : RangeRef -> Integer
  ev-r1 (g) = gr-lo ((g.rr-from).cr-row) ((g.rr-to).cr-row)

  ev-r2 : RangeRef -> Integer
  ev-r2 (g) = gr-hi ((g.rr-from).cr-row) ((g.rr-to).cr-row)

  ev-c1 : RangeRef -> Integer
  ev-c1 (g) = gr-lo ((g.rr-from).cr-col) ((g.rr-to).cr-col)

  ev-c2 : RangeRef -> Integer
  ev-c2 (g) = gr-hi ((g.rr-from).cr-col) ((g.rr-to).cr-col)

  ev-find-col : Program, List Value, Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Integer
  ev-find-col (pg) (vals) (r) (c) (c2) (h) =
    if c > c2 then 0 - 1
    else if ev-show (ev-cell pg vals r c) == h then c
    else ev-find-col pg vals r (c + 1) c2 h

  ev-count-key : Program, List Value, Integer, Integer, Integer, Value, Integer -> Integer
  ev-count-key (pg) (vals) (r) (r2) (c) (key) (acc) =
    if r > r2 then acc
    else if ev-same (ev-cell pg vals r c) key then ev-count-key pg vals (r + 1) r2 c key (acc + 1)
    else ev-count-key pg vals (r + 1) r2 c key acc

  ev-first-key : Program, List Value, Integer, Integer, Integer, Value -> Integer
  ev-first-key (pg) (vals) (r) (r2) (c) (key) =
    if r > r2 then 0 - 1
    else if ev-same (ev-cell pg vals r c) key then r
    else ev-first-key pg vals (r + 1) r2 c key

  ev-lookup : Program, List Value, List Expr -> Value
  ev-lookup (pg) (vals) (args) =
    if list-length args /= 3 then VErr (ev-arity "LOOKUP" 3 (list-length args))
    else if ev-range-arg (list-at args 0) == False then VErr "LOOKUP wants a range like A1:D9 whose first row is the header row"
    else ev-lookup-args pg vals (ev-range-of (list-at args 0)) (ev-expr pg vals (list-at args 1)) (ev-expr pg vals (list-at args 2))

  ev-lookup-args : Program, List Value, RangeRef, Value, Value -> Value
  ev-lookup-args (pg) (vals) (g) (key) (hdr) =
    if ev-is-err key then key
    else if ev-is-err hdr then hdr
    else ev-lookup-bad pg vals g key (ev-show hdr) (ev-range-err pg vals g)

  ev-lookup-bad : Program, List Value, RangeRef, Value, Text, Value -> Value
  ev-lookup-bad (pg) (vals) (g) (key) (h) (bad) =
    if ev-is-err bad then bad
    else ev-lookup-col pg vals g key h (ev-find-col pg vals (ev-r1 g) (ev-c1 g) (ev-c2 g) h)

  ev-lookup-col : Program, List Value, RangeRef, Value, Text, Integer -> Value
  ev-lookup-col (pg) (vals) (g) (key) (h) (col) =
    if col < 0 then VErr ("LOOKUP found no column headed " & h)
    else ev-lookup-rows pg vals g key col (ev-count-key pg vals (ev-r1 g + 1) (ev-r2 g) (ev-c1 g) key 0)

  ev-lookup-rows : Program, List Value, RangeRef, Value, Integer, Integer -> Value
  ev-lookup-rows (pg) (vals) (g) (key) (col) (n) =
    if n == 0 then VErr ("LOOKUP found no row whose key is " & ev-show key)
    else if n > 1 then VErr ("LOOKUP found " & show n & " rows whose key is " & ev-show key & ", and a key that is not unique has no single answer")
    else ev-cell pg vals (ev-first-key pg vals (ev-r1 g + 1) (ev-r2 g) (ev-c1 g) key) col

  ev-if : Program, List Value, List Expr -> Value
  ev-if (pg) (vals) (args) =
    if list-length args /= 3 then VErr (ev-arity "IF" 3 (list-length args))
    else ev-if-on pg vals args (ev-expr pg vals (list-at args 0))

  ev-if-on : Program, List Value, List Expr, Value -> Value
  ev-if-on (pg) (vals) (args) (c) =
    if ev-is-err c then c
    else let t = ev-need-num c "IF"
    in if t /= "" then VErr t
    else if ev-num-of c /= 0 then ev-expr pg vals (list-at args 1)
    else ev-expr pg vals (list-at args 2)

  ev-cond : Program, List Value, Text, List Expr -> Value
  ev-cond (pg) (vals) (nm) (args) =
    if list-length args /= 2 then VErr (ev-arity nm 2 (list-length args))
    else if ev-range-arg (list-at args 0) == False then VErr (nm & " wants a range like A1:B9")
    else ev-cond-on pg vals nm args (ev-expr pg vals (list-at args 1))

  ev-cond-on : Program, List Value, Text, List Expr, Value -> Value
  ev-cond-on (pg) (vals) (nm) (args) (want) =
    if ev-is-err want then want
    else ev-match pg vals (ev-range-of (list-at args 0)) want (nm == "SUMIF")

  ev-concat : List Value, Integer, Integer, Text -> Value
  ev-concat (vs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then ev-lit acc
    else ev-concat vs (i + 1) n (acc & ev-show (list-at vs i))

  ev-text1 : Text, List Value -> Value
  ev-text1 (nm) (vs) =
    if list-length vs /= 1 then VErr (ev-arity nm 1 (list-length vs))
    else ev-text1-on nm (list-at vs 0)

  ev-text1-on : Text, Value -> Value
  ev-text1-on (nm) (v) =
    let bs = text-to-utf8-bytes (ev-show v)
    in let n = list-length bs
    in if nm == "LEN" then VNum (ev-len-of bs 0 n 0)
    else if nm == "UPPER" then ev-lit (utf8-bytes-to-text (ev-fold bs 0 n True []))
    else if nm == "LOWER" then ev-lit (utf8-bytes-to-text (ev-fold bs 0 n False []))
    else ev-lit (utf8-bytes-to-text (ev-slice bs (ev-trim-start bs 0 n) (ev-trim-end bs n) []))

  ev-call : Program, List Value, Text, List Expr -> Value
  ev-call (pg) (vals) (nm) (args) =
    if nm == "SUM" then ev-agg pg vals nm args
    else if nm == "COUNT" then ev-agg pg vals nm args
    else if nm == "MIN" then ev-agg pg vals nm args
    else if nm == "MAX" then ev-agg pg vals nm args
    else if nm == "AVERAGE" then ev-agg pg vals nm args
    else if nm == "IF" then ev-if pg vals args
    else if nm == "SUMIF" then ev-cond pg vals nm args
    else if nm == "COUNTIF" then ev-cond pg vals nm args
    else if nm == "LOOKUP" then ev-lookup pg vals args
    else ev-call-plain pg vals nm args

  ev-call-plain : Program, List Value, Text, List Expr -> Value
  ev-call-plain (pg) (vals) (nm) (args) =
    let vs = ev-args pg vals args 0 (list-length args) []
    in let bad = ev-first-err vs 0 (list-length vs)
    in if ev-is-err bad then bad
    else if nm == "CONCAT" then ev-concat vs 0 (list-length vs) ""
    else if nm == "LEN" then ev-text1 nm vs
    else if nm == "UPPER" then ev-text1 nm vs
    else if nm == "LOWER" then ev-text1 nm vs
    else if nm == "TRIM" then ev-text1 nm vs
    else VErr (nm & " is not a function this sheet knows")

Section: The Expression

  ev-expr : Program, List Value, Expr -> Value
  ev-expr (pg) (vals) (e) = when e
   is ExNum (v) -> VNum v
   is ExText (t) -> ev-lit t
   is ExRef (r) -> ev-cell pg vals (r.cr-row) (r.cr-col)
   is ExRange (g) -> VErr ("a range belongs to a function, and " & (g.rr-from).cr-name & " to " & (g.rr-to).cr-name & " stands where a value was wanted")
   is ExNeg (x) -> ev-negate (ev-expr pg vals x)
   is ExBin (b) -> ev-binary (b.bn-op) (ev-expr pg vals (b.bn-left)) (ev-expr pg vals (b.bn-right))
   is ExCall (c) -> ev-call pg vals (c.cn-name) (c.cn-args)

  ev-negate : Value -> Value
  ev-negate (v) =
    if ev-is-err v then v
    else let t = ev-need-num v "-"
    in if t /= "" then VErr t
    else VNum (0 - ev-num-of v)

Section: Running The Plan

 The values list is filled with zeroes and then written at each entry's
 own index as the derived order reaches it, so a reference resolves to a
 value already computed rather than to a placeholder. `list-set-at`
 writes through the caller's list deliberately here: the list is created
 inside this run and is handed to nobody until the run finishes.

 `list-push` rather than concatenation, and the difference is the whole
 cost of a big sheet: `acc & [x]` repeated n times allocates a fresh list
 of length 1, 2, 3 and so on, which is n squared over two cells and
 17 MB at a thousand. `list-push` extends in place. Every accumulator
 written that way here is created inside its own call from a fresh `[]`
 and is handed to no caller holding an earlier version, which is the
 condition L-ALIAS names; a list living in a record a caller still holds,
 as `pg-cells` does, must keep concatenating.

  ev-zeroes : Integer, Integer, List Value -> List Value
  ev-zeroes (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else ev-zeroes (i + 1) n (list-push acc (VNum 0))

  ev-step : Program, List Value, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Value
  ev-step (pg) (vals) (order) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then vals
    else let v = list-at order i
    in let e = (list-at (pg.pg-cells) v).fc-expr
    in ev-step pg (list-set-at vals v (ev-expr pg vals e)) order (i + 1) n

  eval-run : Program -> Results
  eval-run (pg) =
    let plan = graph-plan pg
    in if plan.pl-ok == False then Results { rs-ok = False, rs-vals = [], rs-msg = plan.pl-msg }
    else ev-run-order pg (plan.pl-order)

  ev-run-order : Program, List Integer -> Results
  ev-run-order (pg) (order) =
    let vals = ev-zeroes 0 (graph-count pg) []
    in Results { rs-ok = True, rs-vals = ev-step pg vals order 0 (list-length order), rs-msg = "" }

  eval-cell : Program, Results, Integer, Integer -> Text
  eval-cell (pg) (rs) (r) (c) =
    if rs.rs-ok == False then "REFUSED: " & rs.rs-msg
    else ev-show (ev-cell pg (rs.rs-vals) r c)

